spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.14841269283480663,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.009757369665746474,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":29.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06808290755018759,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":86.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.05229560613581208,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0016994447615588189,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.16283001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"MetLife, Inc., a financial services company, provides insurance, annuities, employee benefits, and asset management services worldwide. It operates in six segments: Group Benefits; Retirement and Income Solutions; Asia; Latin America; Europe, the Middle East and Africa; and MetLife Holdings. The company offers life, dental, group short-and long-term disability, paid family and medical leave, individual disability, accidental death and dismemberment, accident and health, vision, and pet insurance, as well as prepaid legal plans; administrative services-only arrangements to employers; and general and separate account, and synthetic guaranteed interest contracts, as well as private floating rate funding agreements. It also provides pension risk transfers, institutional income annuities, structured settlements, and capital markets investment products; and other products and services, such as life insurance products and funding agreements for funding postretirement benefits, as well as company, bank, or trust-owned life insurance used to finance nonqualified benefit programs for executives. In addition, it offers fixed, indexed-linked, and variable annuities; pension products; regular savings products; whole and term life, endowments, universal and variable life, and group life products; longevity and funded reinsurance solutions; credit insurance products; accident & health products covering hospitalization, cancer, critical illness, income protection, and scheduled medical reimbursement plans; and protection against long-term health care services. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michel Abbas Khalaf | CEO, President & Director | Compensation: $6.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 46K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MetLife, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $64.5B market cap on $77.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 91% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 82-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 128% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2768681734536025},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 21% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $19.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-19298702.43},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["25 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Eurizon Capital SGR S.p.A. Buys 306,277 Shares of MetLife, Inc. $MET","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/eurizon-capital-sgr-s-p-a-buys-306277-shares-of-metlife-inc-met.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565150.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.93,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Is Drawing Fresh Attention To MetLife (MET)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-met/metlife/news/what-is-drawing-fresh-attention-to-metlife-met","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794544948.028,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.948,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is MetLife (NYSE:MET) Approaching A New High After Strong Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/is-metlife-nysemet-approaching-a-new-high-after-strong-growth","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794505260.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.861,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Pictet Asset Management Holding SA Sells 5,403 Shares of MetLife, Inc. $MET","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/pictet-asset-management-holding-sa-sells-5403-shares-of-metlife-inc-met.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794485933.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MetLife, Inc. $MET Stock Position Cut by International Assets Investment Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/metlife-inc-met-stock-p